[38;5;252m[1m## Harness bug found and fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two issues that were making results unreliable rather than wrong:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mcargo test[0m does not build the [38;5;10mcdylib[0m artifact, so the harness was silently falling back to a stale [38;5;10mtarget/release/libdriver.so[0m. It now builds the cdylib on demand into a separate target directory (avoiding the parent cargo's build lock) and asserts it found a matching artifact.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mstdout[0m capture works by swapping fd 1 process-wide, so the test harness's own progress output from a parallel test thread could land in a capture and cause a spurious mismatch. This actually fired once. [38;5;10mtranslation/.cargo/config.toml[0m now pins [38;5;10mRUST_TEST_THREADS=1[0m, and [38;5;10msession()[0m asserts it rather than failing flakily.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
